<title>BULGARIA: Balkan countries' railways agree united tariffs.</title>
<headline>Balkan countries' railways agree united tariffs.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state railways of several Balkan and Middle Eastern countries have agreed to unify freight tariffs, Bulgarian State Railways General Director Angel Dimitrov said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Dimitrov told a news conference the tariff scheme agreed at a meeting in Istanbul last week would come into effect on February 1 for a one-year initial experimental period.</p>
<p>He said the harmonised tariffs would help increase railway cargo transit from Western Europe to the Middle East via the Balkans.</p>
<p>The countries involved are Yugoslavia, Macedonia, Bulgaria, Romania, Greece, Turkey, Iran and Syria. Hungary has also shown interest in joining the united tariff agreement.</p>
<p>Maximum tariffs are fixed for all countries involved and each country can offer preferential prices, Dimitrov said.</p>
<p>-- Liliana Semerdjieva, Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-84561</p>
